        "original_id": "925d62b2-981b-50ff-bae0-57f2b46e6663",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Shengzhou, Linchuan District, Shaoxing, Fuzhou, Jiangxi, Zhejiang, Hangzhou Bay, Dongyang\n- Systems: Changle River, Lüxi River, Heshan River\n- Concepts: county-level city, district, prefecture-level city\n\nFacts:\n- Shengzhou, formerly called Shengxian or Sheng County, is a county-level city in central Zhejiang south of Hangzhou Bay.\n- Shengzhou is the southeastern part of the prefecture-level city of Shaoxing.\n- Linchuan District is the only district of Fuzhou in Jiangxi, People's Republic of China.\n- Changle River originates from Daoshangling Mountain in Dongyang.\n- Daoshangling Mountain has an elevation of 744 meters.\n- In Shengzhou, the Changle River is known as the Lüxi River and the Heshan River.",
